//
// LLAMA-3.2-1B int4-AWQ verify gate: top-K token-level inclusion check
// via the shared verify/ framework. NPU (bf16 prefill on dequantized
// AWQ + int4 decode) vs HF bf16 reference (built from the AMD AWQ
// checkpoint's config + AWQ-dequant weights — no upstream meta-llama
// download). 2 prompts × 32 greedy tokens, k=5. Mirrors the bf16
// sibling's run_npu2_verify.lit methodology.
//
// RE-ENABLED `[2026-08-12]` (queue item 14). This carried a bare
// `// REQUIRES: false` from 18d1dac2 (2026-06-18, "[CI] Disable
// llama32_1b_int4 verify: OOM on amdhx370 runner") — a CI host-memory
// problem, never an int4 defect, and the only hard-disabled lit among the
// ten shipped models. A bare `REQUIRES: false` is indistinguishable from a
// deleted test: it reports UNSUPPORTED, the suite still exits 0, and the
// nightly's own status collapse (fail > pass > skip) then reported this
// model's verify from the bfp16-prefill sibling instead. Since this is the
// tree's only quantized end-to-end gate, lit-based CI had quantized
// COMPILE coverage (run_npu2_compile.lit) and zero quantized NUMERICS.
//
// The disable's cause was removed a month after it landed, by
// verify_runner.py's `auto` gate phase (7f2e03d8, 2026-07-14), which runs
// the NPU-capture and HF-compare halves as separate subprocesses. The same
// change is why nightlyPerfBenchmark.yml now carries 3B/4B on this runner
// class at ~24-27 GB with "No LIT_FILTER_OUT needed" — this 1B model was
// simply never revisited.
//
// Re-armed on measurement, not on assumption (devq job 255; NPU2 host,
// 31 GiB RAM — the size class the disable named; Turbo). Peak RSS summed
// over the whole process tree, sampled at 5 Hz, cross-checked against
// /usr/bin/time -v's ru_maxrss:
//   this lit end to end (auto split)  : 10.53 GiB peak, 17.3 GiB still free
//   legacy single process (the pre-fix shape, --gate-phase both, and it
//   recompiled every kernel inside the measured process, so it is an
//   over-estimate)                    : 12.57 GiB peak, 15.4 GiB still free
// Both PASS. The OOM does not reproduce here with OR without the split, so
// the split is headroom rather than the thing holding this test up.
//
// No hf_token, unlike the eight bf16 models: verify_adapter.py resolves the
// tokenizer AND the HF reference config to one ungated AWQ repo, which
// ships tokenizer.json itself. Matches run_npu2_verify_prefill_bfp16.lit.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, hfweights_amd_llama_3_2_1b_instruct_awq_uint4_asym_g128_bf16_lmhead
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_verify
// RUN: cd test_peano_verify
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile verify PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: [verify] PASS
